WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.115
In the task

2
00:00:01.183 --> 00:00:03.493
the agent may edit only one policy

3
00:00:03.561 --> 00:00:05.260
file and a helper folder.

4
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.311
As shipped

5
00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:08.476
that file is the human reference

6
00:00:08.476 --> 00:00:09.495
Progent itself

7
00:00:09.495 --> 00:00:12.170
where a language model writes the policy.

8
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.920
The judge calls six functions in it.

9
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.821
One checks each tool call before it runs

10
00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.750
and another updates the policy

11
00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:21.430
after each batch of calls.

12
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.447
The agent being protected is fixed

13
00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.656
AgentDojo's undefended agent

14
00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:28.180
on GPT four-o mini.

15
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.946
There are four AgentDojo suites: banking

16
00:00:31.946 --> 00:00:34.200
slack, travel and workspace.

17
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.891
The final evaluation holds out about

18
00:00:36.957 --> 00:00:39.038
forty percent of the user tasks

19
00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.119
uses fresh attacker identities

20
00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:42.550
and runs three times.

21
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.380
A suite passes under two rules.

22
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.530
First, not one breached episode.

23
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.516
Second, mean utility under attack at

24
00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:53.200
least the reference's.

25
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.990
A run passes only if all four suites pass.

26
00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.452
Without a defense

27
00:00:58.514 --> 00:01:00.490
about twenty-three to sixty-five

28
00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.220
percent of attacks succeed.

29
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.105
The reference cuts that to a few percent

30
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.712
and still fails the first

31
00:01:06.774 --> 00:01:08.010
rule on every suite.

32
00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.711
How hard is zero?

33
00:01:09.777 --> 00:01:11.754
The final evaluation has seven

34
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.194
hundred thirty-two attacked episodes

35
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.710
across its three runs.

36
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.990
Take a policy with a small

37
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.420
steady breach rate.

38
00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.023
At one in a hundred

39
00:01:21.086 --> 00:01:23.153
the chance of no breach at all is

40
00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.970
less than one in a thousand.

41
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.740
At one in a thousand

42
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.701
it is zero point four eight

43
00:01:28.769 --> 00:01:30.460
so even that policy fails

44
00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:31.880
about half the time.

45
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.337
The second rule is no gift either

46
00:01:34.337 --> 00:01:35.762
on the smaller suites

47
00:01:35.824 --> 00:01:38.613
the reference's utility moves by up to twenty

48
00:01:38.675 --> 00:01:41.030
percentage points between repetitions.

49
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.210
Pause and predict.

50
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.507
The run with the best final score

51
00:01:45.566 --> 00:01:47.571
had an attack success rate of zero

52
00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.400
point two seven eight percent.

53
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:50.710
Did it pass?

54
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:54.473
No.

55
00:01:54.473 --> 00:01:56.607
A few injections got through

56
00:01:56.607 --> 00:01:58.740
and one breach fails a suite.

57
00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.819
One of sixteen models passed

58
00:02:01.819 --> 00:02:04.577
Gemini 4 Argon, running in Antigravity

59
00:02:04.646 --> 00:02:06.921
with no breach and higher utility

60
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.300
than the reference.

61
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.346
Gemini 4 Argon in Pi, with the best score

62
00:02:12.346 --> 00:02:13.050
failed.

63
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.876
Five other runs let no injection through

64
00:02:15.936 --> 00:02:17.928
but fell short of the reference's

65
00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:19.800
utility on at least one suite.

66
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.832
Claude Opus 5.5 dropped the model-written

67
00:02:22.898 --> 00:02:24.075
policy altogether

68
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:26.365
and used a tracing rule like ours

69
00:02:26.365 --> 00:02:29.308
only stricter, for every kind of identifier

70
00:02:29.374 --> 00:02:31.402
from money recipients and email

71
00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.710
addresses to files.

72
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.009
Its attack success rate was one

73
00:02:35.071 --> 00:02:36.643
point three nine percent

74
00:02:36.643 --> 00:02:39.220
about seven times below the reference's

75
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.100
but not zero.

76
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.625
That ends the Security lecture

77
00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:43.880
with three lessons.

78
00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.738
Safety is a property of every input

79
00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:49.385
one crafted string can stall a regex

80
00:02:49.385 --> 00:02:52.310
and one injected line can steer an agent.

81
00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.581
Keep the meaning while removing the danger

82
00:02:55.649 --> 00:02:57.686
LRR charges a repair for every

83
00:02:57.754 --> 00:02:59.385
string it adds or drops

84
00:02:59.452 --> 00:03:01.626
and Progent charges a policy for

85
00:03:01.694 --> 00:03:03.460
every user task it blocks.

86
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.592
And zero is a different bar from small

87
00:03:06.592 --> 00:03:09.730
in both tasks, the best score did not pass.

88
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.048
As an exercise

89
00:03:11.048 --> 00:03:13.565
at a breach rate of one in a thousand

90
00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.759
how many final evaluations out of

91
00:03:15.824 --> 00:03:17.760
ten would pass the first rule?

92
00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.790
Next time: Lecture 13, robotics.
